      "body": "Since both MiniWallets start with the same UTXO set and pick the largest coin by default, what about spending the smallest coins which branch B never spends? So a rollback must restore them. Suggestion from my clanker:\n\n```diff\ndiff --git a/test/functional/feature_dbcrash_replay.py b/test/functional/feature_dbcrash_replay.py\nindex dbabb325aa..63ad2bfa30 100755\n--- a/test/functional/feature_dbcrash_replay.py\n+++ b/test/functional/feature_dbcrash_replay.py\n@@ -26,8 +26,10 @@ class ChainstateReplayTest(BitcoinTestFramework):\n         self.log.info(\"Build and flush a short branch on node0 that will be reorged out\")\n         self.disconnect_nodes(0, 1)\n         node_wallet = MiniWallet(node)\n-        for _ in range(2):\n-            node_wallet.send_self_transfer_multi(from_node=node, num_outputs=10)\n+        smallest = sorted(node_wallet.get_utxos(mark_as_spent=False), key=lambda u: (u['value'], -u['height']))[:2]\n+        for u in smallest:\n+            utxo = node_wallet.get_utxo(txid=u['txid'], vout=u['vout'])\n+            node_wallet.send_self_transfer_multi(from_node=node, utxos_to_spend=[utxo], num_outputs=10)\n             self.generate(node, 1, sync_fun=self.no_op)\n \n         self.log.info(\"Restart node0 so that every partial coins batch write crashes\")\n```",
